      "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xR2FFOHpWelY2WlVOd1RFTkVXbWRYUzBjMU9HYxAB&d=17924085&t=1",
      "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xR2FFOHpWelY2WlVOd1RFTkVXbWRYUzBjMU9HYxAB!2m1!1s0x48761ba809fd882b:0x817eee82a924ec96"
    },
    {
      "name": "places/ChIJK4j9CagbdkgRluwkqYLufoE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGUFFVdFlSSFJFZUY5SU1GVnNORGh5YmtnNVlWRRAB",
      "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago",
      "rating": 5,
      "text": {
        "text": "⸻\n\nWe had a mixed experience at this restaurant. The carbonara unfortunately wasn’t great and didn’t quite meet our expectations. However, the atmosphere was amazing , warm, welcoming, and really enjoyable.\n\nWhat truly stood out was the service. The staff were attentive and kind, and the manager was extremely understanding about the issue with the food. They handled the situation professionally and generously didn’t charge us for the carbonara, which we really appreciated.\n\nTo top it off, they even offered us complimentary limoncello shots, which was such a thoughtful gesture.\n\nWhile the food wasn’t perfect this time, the outstanding service and lovely atmosphere would definitely make us consider coming back.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
      "originalText": {
        "text": "⸻\n\nWe had a mixed experience at this restaurant. The carbonara unfortunately wasn’t great and didn’t quite meet our expectations. However, the atmosphere was amazing , warm, welcoming, and really enjoyable.\n\nWhat truly stood out was the service. The staff were attentive and kind, and the manager was extremely understanding about the issue with the food. They handled the situation professionally and generously didn’t charge us for the carbonara, which we really appreciated.\n\nTo top it off, they even offered us complimentary limoncello shots, which was such a thoughtful gesture.\n\nWhile the food wasn’t perfect this time, the outstanding service and lovely atmosphere would definitely make us consider coming back.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
      "authorAttribution": {
        "displayName": "Geni",
        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110073222748837893532/reviews",
        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWQiBWV-iZ39k1I-51ru1ZnkPxWkL5541WQ0adz188-E6wpECc=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3"
      },
      "publishTime": "2026-03-01T23:16:17.107134841Z",
      "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGUFFVdFlSSFJFZUY5SU1GVnNORGh5YmtnNVlWRRAB&d=17924085&t=1",
      "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGUFFVdFlSSFJFZUY5SU1GVnNORGh5YmtnNVlWRRAB!2m1!1s0x48761ba809fd882b:0x817eee82a924ec96"
    },
    {
      "name": "places/ChIJK4j9CagbdkgRluwkqYLufoE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2paU09GRXpaWFZwZFZac1lWWnBla2hrTjBwNGJXYxAB",
      "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago",
      "rating": 2,
      "text": {
        "text": "We ordered a variety of cocktails to start, and the drinks were definitely a highlight. The Mandarin Mojito and Golden Age were both excellent & refreshing, well balanced, and clearly made with care.\n\nStarters were solid overall, with the cheese croquettes standing out as the favourite at the table.\n\nFor mains, we ordered the meatballs and crispy truffle potatoes. Unfortunately, this is where things fell short. The meatball dish arrived as just three meatballs on a bed of spinach with some Parmesan on top, which felt underwhelming for the price. The truffle potatoes were disappointing not crispy at all (despite being described as crispy on menu) and lacking flavour beyond the cheese on top. Another guest ordered the normal potatoes and experienced the same issue, so it didn’t seem like a one off.\n\nFor dessert, we ordered the lemon pie, which was enjoyable, and the remaining desserts were kindly given to us complimentary due to the issues with our main course a gesture we appreciated.\n\nThe manager was fantastic and handled the situation professionally and kindly. However, the waiting staff experience was mixed. When we raised issues, food was taken away without resolution or explanation, and on two occasions staff walked off mid conversation, which felt dismissive and confusing from a customer service perspective.\n\nThat said, the ambience is stunning. The décor is vibrant and immersive, genuinely making you feel like you’re dining on the streets of Italy easily one of the restaurant’s strongest points.\n\nOverall, a beautiful setting with great cocktails and good starters, but inconsistent mains and service prevent it from being the full experience it promises to be.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
      "originalText": {
        "text": "We ordered a variety of cocktails to start, and the drinks were definitely a highlight. The Mandarin Mojito and Golden Age were both excellent & refreshing, well balanced, and clearly made with care.\n\nStarters were solid overall, with the cheese croquettes standing out as the favourite at the table.\n\nFor mains, we ordered the meatballs and crispy truffle potatoes. Unfortunately, this is where things fell short. The meatball dish arrived as just three meatballs on a bed of spinach with some Parmesan on top, which felt underwhelming for the price. The truffle potatoes were disappointing not crispy at all (despite being described as crispy on menu) and lacking flavour beyond the cheese on top. Another guest ordered the normal potatoes and experienced the same issue, so it didn’t seem like a one off.\n\nFor dessert, we ordered the lemon pie, which was enjoyable, and the remaining desserts were kindly given to us complimentary due to the issues with our main course a gesture we appreciated.\n\nThe manager was fantastic and handled the situation professionally and kindly. However, the waiting staff experience was mixed. When we raised issues, food was taken away without resolution or explanation, and on two occasions staff walked off mid conversation, which felt dismissive and confusing from a customer service perspective.\n\nThat said, the ambience is stunning. The décor is vibrant and immersive, genuinely making you feel like you’re dining on the streets of Italy easily one of the restaurant’s strongest points.\n\nOverall, a beautiful setting with great cocktails and good starters, but inconsistent mains and service prevent it from being the full experience it promises to be.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
